{
  "result": "If I had one lever to pull, I wouldn't make everyone agree \u2014 that world would be boring.\n\nI would make curiosity our default instead of judgment.\n\nRight now, when we run into something unfamiliar \u2014 a different opinion, a different culture, a different way of living, someone struggling in a way we haven't \u2014 our first instinct is often fear or judgment. *That's wrong. That's weird. That's a threat.*\n\nI would flip that to: *Huh, that's interesting. How did you get there? What does that feel like?*\n\nBecause almost everything that breaks the world \u2014 polarization, prejudice, conflict, even just people being lonely in the same house \u2014 doesn't come from pure evil. It comes from people being sure they already understand each other when they don't.\n\nIf 8 billion people woke up tomorrow genuinely curious about each other for even 5 minutes a day, we wouldn't automatically solve hunger or climate change or disease, but we would actually be able to work on them together. We'd argue better. We'd learn faster. We'd be a lot less cruel.\n\nThat's the change I'd want. Not enforced kindness, just the real ability to see each other clearly.\n\nWhat would you change?",
